) 31... Bxd1 32. Nxd1 h5 {Being able to play ...h4 at some point and create threats against your opponent's king is usually good. Here it could have been a nice way to look for counterplay.}  
33. Kg1 Qc1 $36 { with ...e3 ideas.} ) 31. Nxd1 {[%eval +1.26][%brsp Qc2]}  Qc7+ 
{[%eval +1.08][%brsp Kh1]}  32. Kg1 $1 {[%eval +1.00][%brsp Qc1]Now there is no need to play g3, like in the 30...Qc7+ line.}  
