Nd6 {[%eval +4.45][%brsp Qd2]}  41. Qd2 {[%eval +4.38][%brsp Ne4]Slowly untangling the position. That is common when you have a lot of additional material but your opponent is active. You have to find space for small improvements and soon the position will play itself.}  
Nc4 {[%eval +4.74][%brsp Qd4]}  42. Qd4 {[%eval +4.84][%brsp Qc1]}  Qc1 {[%eval +4.82][%brsp Kf2]}  
43. Kf1 {[%eval +3.76][%brsp Nxe3]Trying to bring the king closer so White can advance his pawns further.}  
Nxe3+ {[%eval +3.81][%brsp Qxe3]Caruana goes for the queen endgame, that should also be hopeless, but the position is very bad anyway.}  
44. Qxe3 {[%eval +3.83][%brsp Qxd1]}  Qxd1+ {[%eval +3.85][%brsp Kf2]}  45. Kf2 {[%eval +3.87][%brsp Qb1]}  
Qc2+ {[%eval +4.09][%brsp Kg3]}  46. Kg3 {[%eval +4.15][%brsp Qc6]}  g5 {[%eval +4.25][%brsp Kh2]Black does not want to weaken his king, but he's lost otherwise, so he has to try something like this.}  
