Nf6 {[%eval +1.07][%brsp Bc7]}  53. h6 $1 {[%eval +0.72][%brsp Nh7]After patiently making slight improvements to his position, White now plays the very essential swap of pawns on the kingside. It does reduce the material left on the board, but much more importantly undermines the f6-square and as well manages to break through even further with the king.}  
Nh7+ {[%eval +0.78][%brsp Kh4]}  54. Kh5 {[%eval +0.80][%brsp Nf6]}  Nf6+ {[%eval +0.72][%brsp Kg5]}  
