gxh6 {[%eval +0.92][%brsp Kh5]}  57. Kh5 {[%eval +0.94][%brsp Kd7]}  Nf6+ {[%eval +0.88][%brsp Kxh6]}  
58. Kxh6 {[%eval +0.90][%brsp Kd7]}  Ng4+ {[%eval +1.16][%brsp Kg7]}  59. Kg7 $1 
{[%eval +1.28][%brsp Nd4]White has made huge progress, and almost made it look   
   like the position after move 40 was a forced win. But Black's resistance is 
in      no way broken, as the downside of the white  king having reached  g7, is 
 that     the f5-pawn is much harder to  defend and Nakamura instantly tries to  
maximise     his counterplay  against  it.}  Nd4 {[%eval +1.40][%brsp Be4]}  60. 
Be4 {[%eval +1.26][%brsp Nf2]}  Nf2 {[%eval +1.46][%brsp Bb1]}  61. Bb1 $1 {[%eval +1.41][%brsp Ng4]The chessboard is just big enough for the bishop to hide from the black knights while keeping f5 protected.}  
